# What the upload leaves out.
#
# The site serves its own copies of the course material and the timetable
# PDF from website/public, so the copies at the top of the repository are
# duplicates that the build never reads. The launch film is the same: it is
# rendered from its own folder and it is not part of the site.
#
# The leading slash matters. A pattern with no slash matches at any depth,
# and "courses" on its own would take website/src/app/courses with it, which
# is the route the whole course page lives on, and website/public/courses,
# which is every lecture note and handout on the site. A pattern with a
# leading slash is anchored to the top of the repository and leaves those
# alone.
/courses
/docs
/audio

# The notes at the top of the repository, which are for whoever works on
# this and not for whoever reads it.
/MEMORY.md
/report.md

# The build's own scratch, which is never uploaded anyway.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.vercel
**/.git
